# Accessibility for Game Interfaces

Apply this rule when creating or changing a menu, HUD element, or other interface in Godot.

## Controls and navigation

- Every menu must be fully usable with keyboard, mouse, and touch. Give the first control focus when a menu or dialog opens, and keep Tab order logical.
- Focused controls must have a clearly visible focus style.
- Touch targets are at least 44 px high, since the game is playable in a phone browser.
- Never require holding or rapid tapping when a single press would do.

## Feedback and content

- Never communicate meaning by color alone: shortages, idle buildings and terrain also use text, symbols or the inspector.
- Keep text readable at the smallest supported screen size.
- Make status changes understandable: important events (shortages, plague, missed payments, endings) appear in the log and, when they need a decision, in a dialog.
- Player-facing text belongs in `data/*.json` where practical, so it can be edited or translated later.

Do not change unrelated screens solely to meet this rule; mention broader issues to the owner separately.
